Please type the amount you would like to withdraw.

283
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:13,640
Thank you.

284
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:20,240
You want to transfer $10,000 to the World Wildlife Foundation.

285
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:23,200
If this is correct, please press one.

286
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:23,660
No, no.

287
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:24,500
Stupid machine.

288
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,200
What are you doing?

289
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,200
No.

290
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,200
Confirmed.

291
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:28,600
Thank you for using our bank.

292
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,800
Please remove your card from the slot.

293
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:31,500
Goodbye.

294
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:32,680
No way.

295
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:33,380
What happened?

296
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:34,560
Give me my money.

297
00:10:35,830 --> 00:10:36,350
Danger.

298
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:37,400
Danger.

299
00:10:37,810 --> 00:10:43,010
The exits have been sealed and the doors will remain locked until the local authorities arrive.

300
00:10:43,590 --> 00:10:44,730
Thank you for using our bank.

301
00:10:45,210 --> 00:10:45,910
Have a nice day.

302
00:10:46,030 --> 00:10:46,250
No.

303
00:10:52,910 --> 00:10:54,850
All right, Erica, so what about you?

304
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:57,070
Have you ever had any problems with the ATM?

305
00:10:57,770 --> 00:10:59,770
I've had more problems than I can count.

306
00:11:00,350 --> 00:11:00,930
What happened?

307
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:06,110
Well, I think in the last two years, I've probably lost about seven bank cards in an ATM.

308
00:11:06,430 --> 00:11:06,670
Really?

309
00:11:06,950 --> 00:11:08,430
You forget it in the slot?

310
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:09,880
Yes.

311
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:14,400
I leave it in the slot and then walk away from the bank machine and no bank cards.

312
00:11:14,710 --> 00:11:26,250
Well, I think now the ATMs, because this is a common problem, now they have like a little alarm that when you take out your money and everything, it just starts beeping and beeping until you take out your card.

313
00:11:26,490 --> 00:11:26,670
Yes.

314
00:11:26,670 --> 00:11:31,570
And I like the bank machines that actually give you your card first and then give you your money.

315
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:34,270
Because if they give me my money first, that's all I want, right?

316
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:36,990
So I run away with my money and leave my card in the bank machine.

317
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:38,150
Right.

318
00:11:38,170 --> 00:11:39,210
I think that's a good idea.

319
00:11:39,530 --> 00:11:41,130
I've never seen it before, though.

320
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:43,000
In Switzerland, they have them like that.

321
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
In Switzerland.

322
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,800
And I think it's the ATMs that you only have to swipe your card.

323
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:47,140
Oh, yeah.

324
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,820
I've done that as well and also ruined a bank card with that.

325
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:53,880
I swiped it too many times, put in the wrong pin code and...

326
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:54,620
It blocked your card.

327
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:55,880
Yeah.

328
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:56,880
Terrible.

329
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:57,340
Well, what about you guys?

330
00:11:57,880 --> 00:12:02,480
I'm sure everyone has some experience or some inconvenience with ATM machines.

331
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:05,300
So why don't you come to our website and tell us all about it?

332
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:10,700
You can also find lots more resources on our website to help you learn English.

333
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:11,800
So check it out.

334
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,280
And until next time, goodbye!
